      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The aim of this study was to test source modeling strategies for EEG-data from a clinical group of amputees. The experimental conditions (measuring time, age and condition of the patients) resulted in low quality EEG-data. Noise reduction was achieved by a principal component analysis (PCA) and a multiple signal classification (MUSIC). A comparison of the results of these two methods with traditional signal handling yielded superior results for the MUSIC algorithm."},
